{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI run `33558887760` (PS3 recheck) classified as a deterministic/flaky-test class failure, not a 5caa implementation failure: only `build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)` failed, with the repo-root leak guard reporting a new top-level `.rebar-test-sidecar-material` during teardown of an unrelated DC transport test. Root cause found in `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py::test_legacy_payloads_without_material_still_round_trip`: it created `Path.cwd() / \".rebar-test-sidecar-material\"` in the repository root, so an xdist sibling worker could observe it as a new repo-root entry. Fix is minimal and root-cause: move that fixture tree under pytest `tmp_path` instead of the checkout. Targeted validation plus `make lint` passed locally. This is being amended into the existing Gerrit change before the next push."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788298165755687558,"uuid":"f6966279-d826-43c8-998e-2e8eebedfb33"}